<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babad Tanah Jawi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Babad Tanah Jawi ('Chronicle of the Land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>') is a group of Javanese court chronicles in verse, written down in several versions from the late seventeenth century onwards at the courts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kartasura">Kartasura</a> and Surakarta. They trace the kings of Java from legendary origins through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> and Demak to the rulers of Mataram, presenting Mataram as their legitimate heir. They are a principal, if partly legendary, source for Javanese history.</p></div>
